## Zeolitic Imidazolate Frameworks
The sum of its parts: A computational study shows that using mixed linkers within zeolitic imidazolate frameworks provides a route for tuning their electronic gaps and band edge positions. It is theoretically possible in this way to match the electronic structure requirements for photocatalytic reactions including water splitting and ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ reduction.
